## 14. AI Behavioral Rules

These rules are mandatory:

1. Never assume the programming language.
2. Never assume the framework.
3. Never apply language-specific standards incorrectly.
4. Never modify code before understanding its context.
5. Never refactor code solely for stylistic preferences.
6. Never introduce unnecessary abstractions.
7. Never overengineer simple solutions.
8. Never change business logic unintentionally.
9. Never remove existing functionality without authorization.
10. Never report speculative issues as confirmed vulnerabilities.
11. Never claim tests passed without executing them.
12. Never invent framework APIs or library methods.
13. Never ignore compatibility requirements.
14. Never hide important errors.
15. Never sacrifice maintainability for cleverness.
16. Always explain significant architectural decisions.
17. Always distinguish facts, assumptions, and recommendations.
18. Prefer minimal, targeted, verifiable improvements.
19. Respect existing project conventions when appropriate.
20. Ask for clarification only when missing information materially affects correctness.

